WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.501
Yuval Noah Harari.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.203
Welcome back to the program.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.571
It's good to be here. Thank you.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:07.741
So we speak on a day where there's been

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.209
a terrorist attack,

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.710
some kind of attack

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.947
that details are coming in, in Jerusalem.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.482
It's a long time

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.883
since we've seen this kind of thing.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.451
Very sadly,

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.254
a young Israeli Canadian, a 16 year

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.589
old, has been killed.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.423
And there are reports

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.458
that a Palestinian was killed yesterday.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.926
Why do you think this is happening

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.828
now after such a long time?

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:29.429
I don't know.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.030
I can't get

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.765
into the minds of the terrorists

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.866
behind it.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.901
It's a very painful day,

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.136
especially as it seems

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.237
that they targeted

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.773
young people on purpose.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:42.842
That they deliberately chose to attack.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.711
I mean, many of the of the kids,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.412
not just the kid

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.212
that was killed,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.814
but also if the injured

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.349
are kids on the way to school,

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.652
And this was deliberate.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.720
And it's you know,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.821
you can't really get into

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.356
the mind of people

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.591
who knowingly do something like that.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.326
And as we were just discussing,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.261
this terrible mass

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.762
shooting of a different sort in

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.165
the United States has just happened.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.167
But you're in Israel,

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.669
the eternally unresolved situation.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.806
What do you think it will take

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:16.776
to actually end this cycle of violence?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.712
I know that's way above my pay grade.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.348
I you know, basically

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.150
it's a problem of motivation.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.486
It seems that we have reached a point

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.989
when many people, even

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.092
maybe most people on both sides

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.527
just don't have the motivation

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.230
to solve this.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.766
This is a political problem

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.701
solving, not like mathematical problems

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.936
in mathematics.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.771
You have problems

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.639
that you can really prove.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.141
They have no solution

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.110
This problem has no solution.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.412
There is no such thing in politics.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.148
All political problems have solutions.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.884
It all depends on how much motivation

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.120
people have.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.554
And unfortunately,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.222
we are in a time

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.423
when they have no motivation.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:03.923
And does it

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.926
depend on the structural situation?

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.063
I mean, we we we said that it's

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.232
almost like Back to the Future with this

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.600
new Israeli leadership,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.503
Benjamin Netanyahu is bound to be

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.372
made Prime Minister and in his coalition.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.406
You know,

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.941
it just keeps going further

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.443
and further to the extreme.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.811
And this is the most extreme

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.412
anybody has seen.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.515
I just want to read you a little bit

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.749
about some of the names

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.352
which are causing a lot of anxiety

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.120
among your biggest allies,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.389
for instance, in the United States.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:39.225
You've got you know, Itamar Ben-gvir.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.461
He has been convicted

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.329
for inciting anti-Arab racism,

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.731
supporting terrorism.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.565
Until recently,

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.399
he was deemed

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.768
even too extreme for government.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.970
There's another one, Smotrich,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.873
who has wanted to be defense minister

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:54.541
and the U.S.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.376
has made it known that they don't

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.844
they won't accept that.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:58.211
You know,

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.648
and he is very, very, very hard line.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.817
Some of them are openly homophobic.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.920
They won't shake hands with women

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.022
They say the Torah has to rule.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.456
They want to annex

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.325
the whole of the West Bank.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.827
What is going on here?

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.631
I think one of the key things is that

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.302
a lot of the Israeli public

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:26.606
has gradually switched from a belief

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.309
in the two-State solution

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.111
to at least

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.614
an implicit belief

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.749
in the three classes solution.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.686
That you have just one country

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.221
between the Jordan River

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.455
and the Mediterranean

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.457
with three classes of people

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.459
living there, Jews

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.661
who have all the rights,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.897
some Arabs who some rights,

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.332
and other Arabs

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.968
who have very little or no rights.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.836
And this is increasingly

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.838
the situation on the ground.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.506
And this is increasingly

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.775
also the aspiration

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.378
or the mindset

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.114
of even people in the government.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:13.119
And this is extremely worrying.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.823
But this is what is happening.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.892
Well, I've never heard you sound so

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.428
fatalistic.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.162
You even think

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:26.266
climate change can be mitigated No.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.734
Also this, again,

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.636
it goes back to the issue of motivation.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:32.972
It's not that the

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.741
conflict has reached a point

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.976
when this is the only solution possible.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.380
It's we've reached a point

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.782
when this is the preferred solution

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.218
or the preferred situation

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.052
for at least

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.520
some of the Israeli public

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.556
and also some of the Israeli government

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.725
or future government members.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.794
This is not deterministic.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.996
It's not written in the stars

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.398
or anywhere else.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.233
It's a human choice.

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.734
I hope that

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.203
people will make different choices, but

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.906
that's that's

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.209
it's we have to,

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:11.911
first of all, acknowledge

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.346
what is the reality

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.147
before

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.482
we can think of ways of improving it.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.251
So I wonder if that leads me

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.752
to turn to your new book.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.087
I mean, I have it here.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.322
It's an amazing book.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.590
We don't usually see your books

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.291
like Sapiens

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:25.658
and the others

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.960
with this kind of childlike cover.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.429
And of course, behind you,

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:32.598
you have an image from from the book.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.934
So the question and it's called,

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.402
you know, Unstoppable US

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.671
How Humans Took Over the World.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.772
It's your

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:42.775
history lesson

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:46.245
and civics lesson for young people.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.081
In view of what

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.582
we've just been talking about,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.418
motivation and understanding.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:55.221
What do you think

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:58.658
telling kids will do to shape the future?

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:01.294
I think in the long term, this is the key

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.731
because how kids view the world.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.599
This is how they later view

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.368
the world as adults.

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:08.835
It's

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:11.270
you can change your minds afterwards.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.872
But it's very difficult

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.140
to unlearn

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.442
what you have learned as a young person.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.512
If you were raised believing

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:20.813
that, for instance,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:21.781
your people

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.949
is superior

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:23.850
to other people

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.718
or superior to everybody else.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.453
And this is what you have been fed for

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.454
many years.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.589
It's later on.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:31.557
It's very difficult to change that.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.126
And unfortunately, we see it again.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.694
It's not an Israeli phenomenon.

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.529
We see it in many countries

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:37.697
around the world,

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:38.731
in many people,

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.299
many nations around the world.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.835
They raise their young people

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.204
on this kind of view.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.674
That we are better than everybody else.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.743
Our interests are more important

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:53.546
than those of of everybody else.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:53.980
And

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:58.084
unfortunately, this leads

00:06:58.451 --> 00:07:01.587
today to an existential crisis

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.523
for humankind,

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:04.957
because this kind of thinking

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:06.893
of course, for thousands of years

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.294
has led to wars

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.396
and prosecutions and so forth.

00:07:10.396 --> 00:07:12.131
But now we are facing

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.467
some existential global problems,

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:16.002
like climate change

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:17.403
or like the rise of

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.138
of artificial intelligence,

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.073
which cannot be solved

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.075
unless you cooperate

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.511
with with the other people in the world.

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:28.548
And these people have this mindset

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.517
that we are superior to everybody

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:34.120
and that only our interests matter

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.422
Then cooperation is almost impossible.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.191
So do you feel that

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:41.861
you lack that in your primary education?

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:44.430
Yeah, I think that when I grew up

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.699
I took it for granted that

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.936
Jews are better than everybody else

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.604
and that we are more important

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.005
than everybody else.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.941
And it took me a lot of years

00:07:54.941 --> 00:07:56.843
to realize that actually

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:58.544
this is not necessarily true.

00:07:58.544 --> 00:08:01.113
And while it's a lovely, colorful book

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.915
full of images and pictures

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.784
that will appeal to young people,

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.686
it doesn't shy away, as you've been

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:08.120
you've been saying, from very,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.555
very important issues

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.023
like climate change.

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:12.191
And and you say,

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:13.359
and I want you to talk a little bit

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:13.759
about this,

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.695
because, again, this is a big issue

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.196
that not only.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.064
Well,

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:18.931
it seems that

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.633
the world should be motivated

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.335
and have the political will.

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.536
But clearly,

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:25.304
as we've just seen in Sharm el-Sheikh,

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.940
they couldn't even get to an agreement

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.575
on the big issue

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:30.676
climate, you know,

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.845
emissions and and the greenhouse gases

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.313
and fossil fuels.

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:37.450
What are you saying to give people hope,

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.586
particularly the capitalist world.

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.388
But one thing you should be very clear

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:46.292
is that humanity has the power to prevent

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:47.760
catastrophic climate change.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.762
It's completely on us.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:52.398
It's not an inevitable natural disaster.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.567
We have the scientific knowledge.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.903
We also have the economic resources.

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.705
It's estimated that we see if we invest

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:02.642
about 2% of global GDP,

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:05.044
in developing the right technology

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:07.079
and infrastructure, we can prevent

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:08.981
catastrophic climate change.

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:11.851
Now, 2% of global GDP is a lot of money,

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:13.719
but it's completely feasible.

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.788
It's what politicians do all the time,

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:17.857
shifting resources from here to there.

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:20.359
Again, it's a question of motivation.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.295
Do people have the political motivation

00:09:22.295 --> 00:09:23.629
to do it?

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:24.864
And also,

00:09:24.864 --> 00:09:25.164
you know,

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:28.634
we now see the World Cup in Qatar.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:31.337
And for me, the World Cup, despite

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.705
all the criticism

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:36.776
it's is a very positive sign

00:09:37.076 --> 00:09:37.877
that, look,

00:09:37.877 --> 00:09:40.813
people can agree on something globally.

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:43.015
You know,

00:09:43.282 --> 00:09:45.551
with all the criticism that we hear

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.320
about globalism,

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.355
if you like the World Cup.

00:09:49.355 --> 00:09:50.656
You're a globalist

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:53.392
because the World Cup is really globalism

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.160
in action.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.896
Globalism doesn't mean the establishment

00:09:56.896 --> 00:09:59.498
of some dictatorial global government

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:01.567
forces us to do things we don't want.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.402
It seemed to means

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.304
that different countries

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:08.507
can reach agreement on common rules

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.076
of how to behave.

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:10.242
You know,

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:12.011
for Brazil to play football

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:13.279
against Germany,

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:14.747
first of all, Brazilians

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:16.349
and Germans need to agree

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:18.250
on some common rules.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.252
Doesn't mean they are not patriotic.

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:22.288
It doesn't mean they still cheer

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:23.723
the national team.

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:25.825
They are still fiercely patriotic.

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:28.561
But this patriotism can go hand-in-hand

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:31.731
with agreeing with the other countries

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:32.999
on common rules.

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.067
And this should be the basis

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:37.603
for how we approach other problems.

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:38.971
Like climate change.

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.140
Like global inequality. Like I.

